longdesc LaTeX's default style of typesetting mathematics does not
longdesc comply with the International Standards ISO 31-0:1992 to ISO
longdesc 31-13:1992 which require that uppercase Greek letters always be
longdesc typeset upright, as opposed to italic (even though they usually
longdesc represent variables) and allow for typesetting of variables in
longdesc a boldface italic style (even though the required fonts are
longdesc available). This package ensures that uppercase Greek be
longdesc typeset in italic style, that upright $\Delta$ and $\Omega$
longdesc symbols are available through the commands \upDelta and
longdesc \upOmega; and provides a new math alphabet \mathbold for
longdesc boldface italic letters, including Greek. This package used to
longdesc be part of the was bundle, but has now become a package in its
longdesc own right.
